-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Damage Shield, redesigned
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Damage Shield (2, 9): Redesigned. When you deal damage you fortify
--           yourself, shielding yourself for an amount equal to 10/20% of the
--           damage caused. (2 ranks)"
--
-- What it was: deal damage equal to 10/20% of your block value whenever you
-- take or block a melee attack.  That mechanic is not being lost -- it moves
-- to Shield Mastery in woa_2026_08_09_10.sql, which re-points core's
-- spell_warr_damage_shield at 29598/29599.  This file is what takes its place
-- at (2, 9), and the two changes have to land together: the ScriptName DELETE
-- there is what unhooks 58872/58874 from the old behaviour.
--
-- Why swap them at all.  A tier-9 talent that scales off block value duplicated
-- a tier-2 talent that scales off block value, and the tier-9 one was the
-- weaker of the two.  Converting the deep talent into self-healing gives
-- Protection its own sustain that is not the Victory Rush window, and it points
-- at the thing the spec was short of on a solo fork: nobody is healing you.
--
-- DBC layout:
--
--   58872/58874  Effect1 SPELL_AURA_DUMMY, 10 / 20 -- the percentage, read by
--                the script.  ProcFlags changes from 40 (TAKEN) to 20 (DONE):
--                0x4 PROC_FLAG_DONE_MELEE_AUTO_ATTACK
--                | 0x10 PROC_FLAG_DONE_SPELL_MELEE_DMG_CLASS.
--   200649       SPELL_AURA_SCHOOL_ABSORB, MiscValue 127 (all schools),
--                10 seconds.  Base points 0 -- the amount is always supplied by
--                the caster via SPELLVALUE_BASE_POINT0.
--
-- PROC_FLAG_DONE_PERIODIC (0x4000) is deliberately NOT set.  It would let Rend
-- and Deep Wounds feed the shield, which reads well, but with Blood and Thunder
-- (woa_2026_08_09_15.sql) spreading Rend across a whole pack it would mean a
-- spell cast on every tick of every bleed on every target.  Direct damage only.
--
-- 200649's base points are 0, so its tooltip says "Absorbs damage." in prose
-- rather than "$s1".  The amount is written by C++ at cast time, which is the
-- one case where a literal is correct -- a variable would render 0.
--
-- Script: spell_warr_damage_shield_absorb
-- (modules/world_of_alonecraft/src/WarriorDamageShield.cpp).  It exists only to
-- do arithmetic that depends on proc-time state: the damage dealt, the shield
-- already standing (which is added rather than overwritten) and the cap of 10%
-- of maximum health.
--
-- Spells:
--   58872 / 58874 = Damage Shield ranks 1-2
--   200649        = Fortify (the absorb), new
--   59653         = the old Damage Shield damage payload -- still used, now by
--                   Shield Mastery
-- ============================================================

